{title: This Is My Father's World}
{title_ko: 참 아름다워라}
{hymnal: 새찬송가 478장}
{artist: Maltbie D. Babcock / Franklin L. Sheppard}
{genre: Hymn}
{style: Traditional}
{flow: Opening, Meditative}
{key: D}
{key_original: Eb}
{tempo: 84}
{time: 4/4}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[D]This is my Father's [G]world
And [D]to my listening [A]ears
All [D]nature sings, and [G]round me rings
The [D]music [A]of the [D]spheres
[D]This is my Father's [G]world
I [D]rest me in the [A]thought
Of [D]rocks and trees, of [G]skies and seas
His [D]hand the [A]wonders [D]wrought
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[D]This is my Father's [G]world
The [D]birds their carols [A]raise
The [D]morning light, the [G]lily white
De[D]clare their [A]Maker's [D]praise
[D]This is my Father's [G]world
He [D]shines in all that's [A]fair
In the [D]rustling grass I [G]hear Him pass
He [D]speaks to [A]me every[D]where
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[D]This is my Father's [G]world
O [D]let me ne'er for[A]get
That [D]though the wrong seems [G]oft so strong
[D]God is the [A]Ruler [D]yet
[D]This is my Father's [G]world
The [D]battle is not [A]done
Je[D]sus who died shall [G]be satisfied
And [D]earth and [A]heaven be [D]one
{end_of_verse}
